AUDIT NOTE: a systematic fboundp audit over the 978 CL external symbols is
blocked by a packaging quirk — (fboundp 'car) => T but
(find-symbol "CAR" "COMMON-LISP") => NIL and (find-symbol "CAR") => NIL in
COMMON-LISP-USER.  bocl interns kernel symbols where the READER finds them, but
FIND-SYMBOL/packages do not resolve them by package name.  This also affects the
ANSI cl-symbols tests (which use FIND-SYMBOL).  Fixing FIND-SYMBOL/package
membership is a prerequisite for a precise audit and is tracked here.
Remaining: fix find-symbol package resolution, then audit + implement the
missing functions.  Issue kept OPEN.

