PROGRESS (slice 50, v1.1.7):
The FIND-SYMBOL / package-resolution blocker is RESOLVED (true packages, see
bocl-packages memory / closed package work), so the systematic audit was run:
  (do-external-symbols (s "COMMON-LISP") ...)  classifying each by
  special-operator-p / macro-function / fboundp.
Audit result over the 978 external COMMON-LISP symbols:
  579 fbound functions, 72 macros, 25 special operators, 302 not callable.
The 302 are mostly type names, variables/constants, declaration identifiers and
lambda-list keywords (correctly not functions).  After filtering those out, the
genuinely missing FUNCTIONS were implemented (bootstrap/prelude.lisp):
  sinh cosh tanh asinh acosh atanh cis conjugate phase
  logtest ldb-test  ffloor fceiling fround ftruncate
  constantp compiled-function-p function-lambda-expression
  truename file-author get-decoded-time clear-output
All verified (hyperbolic inverses round-trip; cis/conjugate use kernel COMPLEX;
ffloor&co. return float quotients; constantp on self-eval/quote/keywords).

